    "word_count": 69,
    "first_person_markers": 5,
    "text": "i filled a cup before checking whether anyone was thirsty. then i became irritated that nobody drank. the cup was doing fine; my expectation was leaking all over the table. i emptied it and asked a question. making something for people is easier when you occasionally permit the people to describe what they need. this is a radical method, and i understand why some important builders find it unsettling."
  },
